# Build-context filter for website/Containerfile, the only image the repo
# builds. It lives at the repo root because that is the build context (see the
# Containerfile header) and podman reads .containerignore from the context
# root. Docker does not read this file at all; build with podman.
#
# Deny everything, then re-admit the two directories the build needs;
# otherwise the Swift sources and the ~1GB GhosttyKit.xcframework ride along.
*
!website/
!assets/

# Regenerated inside the image by `bun run build` — never copy a host build in.
website/node_modules/
website/public/docs/
website/public/tailwind.css
website/public/sitemap.xml
website/public/robots.txt

website/Containerfile
**/.DS_Store
